# Documentation

Update the matching doc in the same change as the code.

- Product, UX, or field-rule changes → `docs/business.md` (no stack names).
- Architecture, env, modules, Docker, tests, CI → `docs/implementation.md`.
- Meaningful AI-assisted work → `AI.md` (what was generated, kept, rejected, and why).

`implementation.md` and `.env.example` must match what exists now. Do not describe unbuilt code. Do not duplicate architecture into `README.md`; the README routes and shows how to run.
